## 6. Novelty/prior-art status

Important scope correction: the base `Q_k` Fourier equivalence and rank formula are known in equivalent form in marginal/contingency-table literature. Barak et al. (PODS 2007) explicitly state Fourier sufficiency/necessity for marginals and the `sum_{j<=k} C(n,j)` coefficient count. Current work by Lebeda-Nikolov-Tang (2025/26) uses the same marginal/Fourier framework.

Boolean low-frequency uniqueness is also active: Vershynin (2024) and Chen (2026) study/resolve generic thresholds near `n/2`.

The exact GF(2)-rank threshold theorem above was not located in a targeted current search, but its components are elementary. Status: **potentially new combination/corollary; priority unresolved**. Do not claim novelty yet.

A second useful bridge is that Boolean `Q_k` collisions are simple `[k]`-trades; known trade theory gives minimum collision Hamming distance `2^(k+1)`.

